SLLM patch 13 (phase2-fuse): fused small ops, bitwise the ggml kernels they replace. Four new entries in ggml-metal's
fusion table (so the graph optimizer keeps them adjacent), their checks, encoders in ggml-metal-ops.cpp and kernels in
kernels/prefill.metal:
- RMS_NORM + MUL + ROPE (NEOX): the q head norm and rope in one pass (Qwen3, Gemma-3 q);
- RMS_NORM + MUL + ROPE (NEOX) + SCALE: the same with the q scale (Gemma-3);
- RMS_NORM + MUL + ROPE (NEOX) + VIEW + SET_ROWS (f16): the k head norm, rope and cache write in one pass;
- ADD + RMS_NORM + MUL: a residual add and the next norm (the sum stays an output).
Each kernel repeats the per-element arithmetic of kernel_rms_norm_mul_f32_4, kernel_rope_neox_f32, the scale unary
and kernel_set_rows (f32 -> f16) with the norm's reduction structure; the encoders use ggml_metal_op_norm's own
thread count and fall back to the unfused ops when it does not fit. SLLM_FUSE=0 turns all four off; status export
ggml_backend_metal_sllm_fuse_status (dispatch count).
Against llama.cpp b11669 (source tarball 620d222) after patches 0001..0011 (0012 is left to the qmm work), applied with
patch -p1 in ggml/.

